xmodel/as109-bounded-y6-chain-review-grok-20260824.md:193:(1,6)  affine triangular automorphism
xmodel/as109-bounded-y6-chain-review-grok-20260824.md:200:Thus a `(6,6)` Keller pair cannot land on `(0,6)`, `(4,6)`, or `(5,6)`, and must land on `(1,6)`, `(2,6)`, or `(3,6)`, all of which are automorphisms after the reviewed quintic range. There is no hidden third sextic case such as a residual `(6,6)` after `GL_2`, a mixed `(6,r)` that is not a swap of `(r,6)`, or an imprimitive `(6,6)` needing its own normal form.
