xmodel/subrect-orbit-bridge-check-grok46-20260902.md:129:A two-root top form composed with an automorphism: `(x,xy)` after a linear source change `(x,y)↦(y,x)` remains `nu=2`; after nonlinear `E_2` it becomes `nu=1` and `D` rises. Affine preserves `nu`; nonlinear shears on a two-root rectangle raise `D` and can drop `nu` to 1. That is why a one-root representative in an Aut×Aut orbit is never `D`-minimal once a two-root (subrectangular) representative exists, which vdE supplies for every counterexample.
