xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:30:**F1. Schenk, *A valuation-theoretic proof of the Jacobian conjecture in dimension two*, Zenodo 18622130, 2026-02-12.** Unchanged: created 2026-02-12, updated 2026-02-13, one file `Jacobi in N=2.pdf`. SHA-256 this session `6ba4088386eb40affbb4abad54bb8e1574de09d00da9d1fbeac9f5c88d160f24`. Scoop-claim of JC2 over algebraically closed char 0 via Stein factorization, affine-dicritical Rees degeneration, positivity of the Jacobian two-form, triviality of finite étale covers of \(\mathbb{A}^2\), Zariski’s Main Theorem. **Scoop-claim of the whole plane problem, not a THREAT** to N\(\le 5\), the cusp theorems, or the two curve kills. Not audited here.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:32:**F2. Xavier, *An organizing principle in the study of the Jacobian Conjecture*, arXiv:2606.22041v1, 2026-06-20.** SHA-256 `204357fbba319fb7ac4b6d49055234df20f7a7f3eb927b6dda585a876a98c573` (6 pp.). For an irreducible component \(\Omega\) of \(\{\deg F\le k,\;\det DF=1\}\), either \(\Omega\subset\mathrm{Aut}(\mathbb{C}^n)\) or the general member of \(\Omega\) is not an automorphism. Recorded in the 08-16 JC sweep. **STRUCTURE** as a dichotomy; no plane decision. **IRRELEVANT** as a close or threat.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:34:**F3. Adamus–Hajto, *On the Jung–van der Kulk decomposition into Pascal finite factors*, arXiv:2607.09340v1, 2026-07-10.** SHA-256 `3e7c10f7c1c322ffe1a61d8f328b6ae14b63ff5bba269f716fcaf34d0cdb250a`. Every plane automorphism fixing the origin factors as a diagonal Jacobian times Pascal-finite automorphisms; \(\det J_F=1\) iff \(F\) is a composition of Pascal-finite maps, in any characteristic. An analogue of the Exponential Generators Conjecture in dim 2. **IRRELEVANT** to noninvertible Keller maps; it classifies automorphisms.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:36:**F4. Jelonek–Menani–Michalska, *On Buzzard's Theorem*, arXiv:2608.17166v1, 2026-08-17.** SHA-256 `6f64b8f7b0c10ac287cff0e5ed1de985389509b5bb9004e468baf150519417ff`. Over any infinite field, for \(n\ge 2\), there exist Jacobian-one polynomial automorphisms with prescribed values and prescribed SL differentials at finitely many distinct points. **IRRELEVANT** (constructs automorphisms).
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:38:**F5. Kowalczyk, *A note on the real Jacobian conjecture in degree 7*, arXiv:2608.12294v1, 2026-08-12.** SHA-256 `101c3d50e88921156b116260825ba79e9cdc8241536172c9eb72a0f0927f7672`. Real JC for \(\deg p=7\) with leading form \(\alpha x^7+\beta x^6 y\); no atypical pairs with \(\deg p=7\) and \(\deg q\) even and coprime to 7. **IRRELEVANT** to complex JC2.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:40:**F6. Braun–Gwoździewicz–Fernandes–Oréfice-Okamoto, *A sharp degree bound in the real Jacobian conjecture*, arXiv:2605.12302v2, 2026-05-24.** SHA-256 `f1aa8f3416bd2bf17afe271100b3b08391952597f0736a2921057a518e9d3d5f`. Real plane maps with nowhere-zero Jacobian: injective if \(\deg p\le 6\); a noninjective example at \(\deg p=7\). Settles the real degree bound. **IRRELEVANT** to complex JC2 (Pinchuk-type real maps already have nonconstant Jacobian over \(\mathbb{C}\)).
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:42:**F7. Prellberg, *Collision-generated compression for homogeneous Keller maps*, arXiv:2608.12543v2, 2026-08-31 (v1 2026-08-12).** SHA-256 of fetched v2 PDF `82dd331e72887cbe88c0923cacdb8a717015ccb0cf4645550f0b8b45d4e23c44`. Polarization-algebra compression of high-dimensional homogeneous Keller maps (Thompson 24-var cubic; van Rijn 19-var). Produces a 38-variable Hessian-nilpotent quartic violating Zhao’s vanishing conjecture. **IRRELEVANT** to the plane; **STRUCTURE** only as language for collisions of homogeneous Keller maps.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:44:**F8. Window recap already hashed 2026-09-01 (no new versions this session).** Kistner–Shaska 2608.02863 (graded dim-3; Prop. 3.21: no cyclic-cone descent to a two-variable Keller pair); Gao 2608.00222 (\(n\ge 3\)); Mondello 2608.02634 (char-2 plane); Shaska 2607.20210v2 (every graded plane Keller map is an automorphism); Jelonek 2607.20597; van Dobben de Bruyn 2608.27341; Pissolato 2608.19069; Migus 2607.21572v3 (real Keller maps with non-dense image; \(S_2\subseteq\{2m:m\ge 3\}\) and JC2 \(\Rightarrow S_2=\emptyset\)). SuperMind HEAD `8b376296` (2026-08-05) unchanged. Strinz `(75,125)` HEAD `16ae8b263cb8` (2026-08-30) unchanged. Helali Zenodo 21479814 v1.0.1 (2026-07-21) unchanged. Kakarottoooo public-preprint-v1 (2026-08-10) unchanged. Roy van Rijn HEAD `43028937` (2026-09-02) is lattice-foundry / Elkies rank-17 / Q80 work, not a plane Keller claim.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:46:**F9. Borisov–Gabber–Vasiu, *Infinite transitivity of tame groups of automorphisms of affine spaces*, arXiv:2609.00391v1, 2026-09-02.** SHA-256 `32e2dd12dae4e772f5ea9ecac6401edd893c772abb61e4184ff973e8897bfd82` (202 pp.). Tame automorphisms over finite fields acting on ordered point-sets; complexity measured by \(\max(\deg F,\deg F^{-1})\). **IRRELEVANT** to JC2 (automorphism group, finite fields).
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:48:**F10. Shaska, *Deciding superellipticity and computing the Weierstrass normal form*, arXiv:2609.00672v1, 2026-09-02.** Algorithm deciding whether a plane model is birational to \(y^n=h(x)\). **IRRELEVANT** to Keller maps.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:58:**F11. Corral–Gómez-Martínez–Senovilla-Sanz, *Cuspidal dicritical foliations and analytical invariants of cusps*, arXiv:2605.30634v1, 2026-05-28.** SHA-256 `d3bc4da7093756084cada50f9eb0a90344d9108aae488454fcb42b999e176cd1`. Local germs of foliations on \((\mathbb{C}^2,0)\): a foliation is *cuspidal dicritical* if after the minimal resolution of a cusp it is totally \(E\)-dicritical along the cuspidal divisor. The invariant curves through free points of \(E\) are equisingular cusps, not in general analytically equivalent. Main theorems: \(\ell\)-transversality with a minimal standard basis of 1-forms freezes the first \(\ell+2\) generators of the semimodule \(\Lambda_C\) of differential values; a bound on the divisorial value \(\nu_E(\omega_{\mathcal{F}})\) in terms of the conductor of \(\Lambda_C\) forces \(\Lambda\)-constancy of the whole family. Explicit conductor formula \(c(\Lambda_C)=\tilde u_{s+1}-n-m+1\). **STRUCTURE** for the local analytic classification of one-Puiseux-pair branches and for the vocabulary “dicritical along a cusp.” **IRRELEVANT** as a close of Domrina–Orevkov or of a global polynomial Keller map: these are local foliations, not polynomial self-maps of \(\mathbb{A}^2\), and the Jacobian of a Keller map is a *constant*, not a foliation 1-form.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:60:**F12. Artal Bartolo–Veys, *Dicritical divisors and hypercurvettes*, arXiv:2505.24648v1 (hashed 2026-09-01 `cdbb75f8…`).** Local existence of prescribed dicriticals in dim \(\ge 3\). Already registered. **STRUCTURE** for the word; **IRRELEVANT** to global plane Keller dicriticals.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:64:No post-2020 source found that produces, or forbids, a \(\mu=1\) affine-image dicritical for an irreducible-\(A_F\) plane Keller map, or that repairs/extends Domrina I–II / Domrina–Orevkov beyond the campaign’s own replays. Orevkov’s 2025–2026 papers are germs ramified over \(u^{d_1}=v^{d_2}\) (F14), a degree-10 triple-point construction (F25), and real-quartic arrangements relative to three lines (arXiv:2607.19457v2, SHA-256 `6f225cbf8f682d28af1f6d3736d005044f3dbd0f2670ef70440bc7846e7eecdb`, **IRRELEVANT**), not a low-degree Keller classification. **`OPEN[RESIDUAL-TO-DOMRINA-STATE]` stands.**
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:96:**F21. McDaniel, *Some remarks on Hessians and Wronskians*, arXiv:2607.12162v1, 2026-07-13.** SHA-256 `cb43074e429e96e0b7a5e8051e716fd294245b7f1e3bfbb7eab6c92d94f19747`. \(W\)-polynomials of subspaces of homogeneous bivariate forms; a proof of Iarrobino’s strong Lefschetz theorem in codimension two. **IRRELEVANT** to unit Wronskians of univariate polynomials.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:98:**F22. Grabowski, *On algebraic integrability of vector fields with rational function coefficients that separate variables*, arXiv:2609.00974v1, 2026-09-02.** SHA-256 `442cc9a3374878e301bbd3a219a383472cb23dad89b5623a39493bf929a6b7ab`. Necessary and sufficient condition for a variable-separating rational vector field to have a maximal-dimensional ring of rational first integrals, via reduction modulo almost all primes (Grothendieck–Katz \(p\)-curvature for this class), plus explicit formulae for the integrable coefficients. **STRUCTURE** for polynomial/rational ODE degree-termination in the *separable* class; the A2 3\(\times\)3 Wronskian system on the E1-wall is not a separated-variables vector field. **IRRELEVANT** as a close of `OPEN[A2-U-BOUND]`.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:114:**F25. Orevkov, *On curves of degree 10 with 12 triple points*, arXiv:2601.07809v3, 2026-02-09.** SHA-256 `6cedc659d9cb1bb52380a761f51d7380dcf0a41d5aaef9844c2ee3a5cda56d22`. Constructs an irreducible *rational* degree-10 curve with 12 triple points, and a union of three rational quartics with 19 triples; counterexamples to a Dimca–Harbourne–Sticlaru conjecture; an analytic family degenerating to the dual Hesse arrangement plus a line. **IRRELEVANT** to one-place-at-infinity polynomial curves (these are multi-place projective curves with triples, not AM semigroups).
