xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:9:The algebraic recursion and generated Singular contracts are source-complete, but the AWS custody path is not safe for a pilot. The late authority accepts an allowlisted copied candidate without binding it to the independent classifier output, and it reads that live candidate only after freezing the terminal archive. A bounded no-verdict candidate can therefore be replaced by the dead or survivor string and promoted; the public marker can also disagree with the reviewed archive. Dynamic stage records are not bound to the current job identity/nonce or regenerated by the classifier, and the supervisor has no fail-safe containment on supervisor `SIGKILL`/death. These are promotion and custody defects, not residual mathematical uncertainty.
xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:11:No AWS launch is authorized by this review. No canonical source was edited, no commit/push was made, no AWS or web operation was performed, and no local Singular, msolve, Sage, PARI, or other heavy CAS was run.
xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:89:The first two are rebound to the archived `NODE_INPUT.json` and independently reconstructed from the frozen `work/base` source. The third is rebound to the exact witness row/column selection and literal. The witness script has the exact ring once, the 95-pivot gate once, the determinant replay once, exact equality/NF-stability gates, forms exactly `SUCCESSOR_IDEAL=(g1,g2,Delta_node1)`, and has zero `sat(` calls and zero node-1 power loops. The recursor byte-compares the replayed standard basis, pivot log, and residual to the R3 archive before using the run. The actual Singular replay remains live-host debt; no success is claimed locally.
xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:95:The builder also regenerates the archived node-1 reduce and size-6 census scripts byte-for-byte. The host witness stage reruns the reducer and selected determinant. The production phrase “replays rank provenance” should not be read as rerunning the older rank archive's Singular computation: `verify_rank_bound` hash-checks and parses that frozen certificate. The independent support calculation above supplies the missing non-CAS rederivation of its structural upper-bound content.
xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:127:The saturation stage's certified open standard basis is byte-compared to the chart's independently recomputed active standard basis. This cross-stage equality supplies the chart with the repaired saturation certificate even though the chart template itself does not duplicate the reverse-power block. Actual Singular execution is still required on the live pinned host.
xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:145:`run_singular_stage.py` checks live PGID/SID and writes an identity JSON, but the result JSON does not hash that identity or bind the job tag, lease, worker/supervisor start times, expected PGID/SID, Singular binary digest, or source archive. `Recursor.run_stage` records only node, stage, return code, timeout, script hash, and stdout hash. `classify_resume.stage_lines` checks only self-consistency of script/stdout/stderr/result hashes; it neither requires the identity file nor regenerates dynamic reduce/rank/saturation/chart scripts from the frozen builders.
xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:147:The accepted synthetic fixtures prove the gap: arbitrary one-line fixture scripts and no identity files pass the real dead/survivor classifier when paired with fabricated marker transcripts and matching self-hashes. Required repair: make the classifier regenerate and byte-compare every dynamic script and required artifact set, verify current-job identity JSON and its hash from each result, verify runner/child starttime/uid/PGID/SID/job tag/cgroup/cap/argv/Singular digest, and reject copied or missing identities. The bounded no-verdict chain must likewise be compared to the driver's exact remainder literals, hashes, bound, stage sequence, and reason.
