xmodel/nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:63:After killing `t^{d−1}` in `p` by a shift of `t`, and using affine automorphisms that preserve the pair `(d,n)` — namely `(x,y)↦(αx+δ y+μ, βy+ν)` with `α,β∈ℂ^*` — the residual coefficient space has dimension `d+n−4` (count: `d` lower terms of `p` plus `n` of `q`, minus shift of `t`, minus two translations, minus the already-used leading-monic scaling). For `(8,6)` this is 10; for `(9,6)` this is 11. Only *odd* coefficients of the leading relation control `β_1`; even coefficients are absorbed. Dimensionality therefore does not obstruct any of the six types. A symmetric (even/odd) ansatz can force coincident pairs or a gcd-2 cover; failure of a symmetric ansatz is not a non-realisation theorem.
