xmodel/schenk-audit-b-sol56-20260901.md:189:From that conditional birationality, Keller makes \(F\) étale and hence quasi-finite. Zariski’s Main Theorem makes it an open immersion after the finite birational intermediate model is identified with the normal target. The paper’s Lemma 12.2 is false, and its proof of Lemma 12.3 misses codimension-two complements, but the required \(\mathbb A^2\)-specific conclusion is repairable: a divisorial complement gives a nonconstant unit on an alleged copy of \(\mathbb A^2\); a codimension-at-least-two complement has the same global coordinate ring by normality and cannot itself be affine with that spectrum unless it is all of \(\mathbb A^2\). Thus a birational Keller map would indeed be an automorphism.
