xmodel/max12-912-order3-d1-double-root-toric-blowup-source-review-grok-20260825.md:257:`eliminate` on an already-computed standard basis is valid Singular semantics: `eliminate(I, var)` recomputes a Gröbner basis of the ideal `I` with respect to an elimination order and returns the elimination ideal. The current ring order is in fact already an elimination order for `u` (`u` is the largest variable), and after `u` is absent from generators it is an elimination order for `v`. Either way the call is legal.
