xmodel/max12-812-order2-square-lowcontact-c1-c2-localized-review-grok-20260826.md:158:What is proved is exact ideal membership of `C14-(3/8)E^2` in `sat(c2G,(p k0))`, plus the integral `c=1` membership of `C12-(3/8)E^2` in `c1G`.  Neither test uses `radical()`.  Saturation commutes with taking points of `D(p k0)`: a point with `p k0≠0` lies on `V(c2G)` iff it lies on `V(sat(c2G,(p k0)))`.  It does not radicalize, and it does not assert that the quotient is reduced.
