xmodel/max12-912-squarefree-poisson-truncation-review-grok-20260825.md:351:**General induction, at reduced-point scope only.** Let `R^{(s)}` be the truncation of `R` through a given pole order, with two consecutive depressed remainders `(\Gamma,\Delta)` encoding the failure of the next coefficients to be polynomial. Then the next nonnegative piece of `R^4` has pole numerator proportional to `\Gamma\Delta` (or a fixed cubic form in `(\Gamma,\Delta)` over one extra power of `K`). Squarefreeness of `K` converts `K\mid\Gamma\Delta` into an eight-way allocation, and the following row’s cubic remainder vanishes on each line `\ell_i` only if both remainders vanish there. Resonances are admitted only at Q-degrees in `{9,6,3,0}`, and only `lambda` and `delta` are polynomial target automorphisms. The induction still has to reach `T_{-7}` and the constant Jacobian; four confirmed bands do not finish it.
