xmodel/max12-812-order2-square-d1-a9-d23-j38-r3-tail-hostile-review-grok-20260826.md:273:Division by `sigma^{38}` is polynomial-ring division of an element of `(sigma^{38})`. The grade-38 coefficient is `-J/4`. Adjoining `iJ*J-1` produces the ideal `(-J/4, iJ J-1)` in the polynomial ring over `Q`. Then `J` lies in the ideal because `4` is a unit, and `1 = iJ·J - (iJ J-1)` lies in the ideal. The compiled test is `reduce(1, std(ideal(subst(q38,sigma,0), iJ*J-1)))==0` before radicals.
