+The requested single negative control combining "two points at infinity" with
+both coordinate degrees `>=6` is not available for a genuine polynomial
+automorphism: by the Jung-van der Kulk triangular normal form, if both
+coordinate degrees are greater than one, their highest homogeneous parts are
+powers of one linear form, so the two coordinate curves have the same point at
+infinity.  This blocks promotion, not the computation.
