+BASIS_BEGIN
+G[1]=1
+BASIS_END
+MAIN_SATURATED_EMPTY
+```
+
+Runtime was 2.99s.  Empty-wrapper, nonempty-wrapper, and unsaturated-nonunit
+controls all passed.
+
+Automorphism controls:
+
+* Degree `>=6` triangular automorphism:
+  `F=x+y^6`, `G=y+(x+y^6)^7`, `J(F,G)=1`, degrees `(6,42)`.  This survives the
+  direct global Jacobian check, but both top forms are powers of `y`; it is not
+  a two-infinity-point control.
+* Two-infinity-point automorphism:
+  `f=A*x+y`, `g=C*x+y`; the top lines are distinct when `A!=C`, and
+  `A=2,C=1` gives `J=1`.  This has degree `(1,1)`.
+
+The requested single negative control combining "two points at infinity" with
+both coordinate degrees `>=6` is not available for a genuine polynomial
+automorphism: by the Jung-van der Kulk triangular normal form, if both
+coordinate degrees are greater than one, their highest homogeneous parts are
+powers of one linear form, so the two coordinate curves have the same point at
+infinity.  This blocks promotion, not the computation.
+
+## FALLACY-v2 Scope
+
+No exit-price assertion is made; no `charge_basis` line is licensed.
