@@ -0,0 +1,369 @@
+# `(99,66)` delta `5/2` joint high-`z` computation
+
+## Verdict
+
+`OPEN[DELTA-5/2-FULL-JOINT-NOT-KILLED]`.
+
+The executable Prop. 6.2 high-`z` joint systems built here are nonunit through
+depth 6 over `GF(32003)`, `GF(32009)`, `GF(32027)`, and `Q`.  There is no
+`[1]` certificate for `delta=5/2`, so `delta=5/2` is **not** dead from this
+computation and `(99,66)` is **not** reduced to Moh branch B here.
+
+This is a bounded necessary calculation, not a Keller pair and not a full
+polynomial-pair lift.  The missing full pieces are the lower `z` bands, the
+effective `T2,T3 in K[f,g]` recurrences, the major `4/9` centre, and Moh's
+unprinted 11-variable elimination.
+
+Artifacts:
+
+```text
+box/g9966d52-20260903/g9966_delta52_joint_driver.py
+box/g9966d52-20260903/g9966_delta52_joint_results.json
+box/g9966d52-20260903/delta52_highz_depth{4,5,6}_{F32003,F32009,F32027,Q}.sing
+box/g9966d52-20260903/delta52_highz_depth{4,5,6}_{F32003,F32009,F32027,Q}.log
+box/g9966d52-20260903/control_moh1612_appendixII_Q.sing
+box/g9966d52-20260903/control_moh1612_appendixII_Q.log
+box/g9966d52-20260903/artifacts.sha256
+```
+
+## Custody
+
+The lane receipt `xmodel/g9966-delta52-joint-gpt55-20260903.run.v2` was parsed
+mechanically.  The manifest was generated from its indexed
+`charged_input_<i>_basename=` and `charged_input_<i>_sha256=` fields; no digest
+from the prompt was retyped.  The command wrote the derived manifest outside
+the read-only lane input directory and ran `sha256sum -c`.
+
+All ten frozen inputs under `/tmp/jc2-lane.gSx1Ze/inputs` returned `OK`:
+
+```text
+g9966-source-review-opus5-20260903.md
+xu-delta52-lift-gpt55-20260903.md
+moh9966-B-lift-sol56-20260903.md
+moh9966-branchB-sol56-20260903.md
+xu9966-read-gpt55-20260903.md
+triangular_preprocess.py
+moh1983_jram340_configurations_of_roots.pdf
+xu2016_intersection_numbers_split_minor_roots_arxiv1604.07683v4.pdf
+FALLACY-v2.md
+g9966rev_driver.py
+```
+
+## Moh Source Read
+
+Moh page images were generated and named:
+
+```text
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p190_pdf51.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p191_pdf52.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p192_pdf53.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p193_pdf54.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p194_pdf55.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p195_pdf56.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p196_pdf57.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_pp190_196_pdf51_57.txt
+```
+
+Read facts:
+
+* p.190 defines the minor-disc branch by the multiplicity inequality against
+  `d_r/(n-M_r)`.  For `(99,66)`, the charged skeleton has `d_3=11`,
+  `n-M_3=2`, so the threshold is `11/2`; `u_3=3` is the minor side and
+  `v_3=8` is the major side.
+* pp.191-193 prove Prop. 6.1.  Read on the minor side with `V_r=u_s=3`,
+  `delta_3=-1`, and `n/d_3=9`, the order identity is
+  `ord g(sigma)=n*delta_3+u_s*(n/d_3)*(delta-delta_3)
+  = -99+27(delta+1)=9(3delta-8)`.  Thus the detector ceiling is
+  `delta<8/3`.
+* p.194 gives the coordinate setup.  The top form is
+  `[(y-a x)^v_s (y-b x)^u_s]^(n/d_s)` with `a != b`; after choosing the major
+  direction so `a=0`, Moh defines `z=y-bx-e`.
+* p.195 states Prop. 6.2:
+  `deg_y Gbar=v_s*n/d_s`, `deg_z Gbar=u_s*n/d_s`, and for `i<s`,
+  `deg_y Tbar_i^psi=v_s*(-mu_i)/d_s`,
+  `deg_z Tbar_i^psi=u_s*(-mu_i)/d_s`.
+* p.196 proof uses the same expression `Gbar=sum a_ij y^i z^j` and the total
+  degree condition `i+j<=n`.
+
+For `(99,66)`, `d_s=11`, `v_s=8`, `u_s=3`, `-mu_1=66`, `-mu_2=55`.
+Therefore N14 is:
+
+```text
+Fbar=T_1^psi in span{y^i z^j: 0<=i<=48, 0<=j<=18, i+j<=66},
+  corner y^48 z^18.
+
+Gbar in span{y^i z^j: 0<=i<=72, 0<=j<=27, i+j<=99},
+  corner y^72 z^27.
+
+T2bar in span{y^i z^j: 0<=i<=40, 0<=j<=15, i+j<=55},
+  corner y^40 z^15.
+```
+
+`T3` is not in Prop. 6.2's printed range (`i<=s-1`), so I did not put a Prop.
+6.2 box on `T3`.
+
+## Branch Data
+
+The charged Opus review §3-§7 was read first.  Its Galois argument is the one
+used here: at ramification denominator `e=2`, the Galois action sends
+`pi -> -pi` and must preserve the root multiset with multiplicities.  A
+`[2,1]` multiset cannot be stable because both the double and simple fixed
+root would have to be `0`.  Thus the `delta=5/2` split is forced to
+`[1,1,1]` with
+
+```text
+p(pi)=pi(pi^2-c),  c != 0.
+```
+
+The gauge `pi -> lambda*pi` sets `c=1`.  I kept a variable `split_c` in the
+Singular localizer and imposed `split_c-1`; saturation used
+`T*gamma*split_c-1`, so both the split scale and Jacobian scalar are localized.
+
+Fixed by the skeleton/source read:
+
+| item | value | source |
+|---|---|---|
+| degrees | `(n,m)=(99,66)` | charged `(99,66)` row |
+| gcd chain | `d=(99,33,11,1)` | charged Moh/Xu skeleton |
+| final major data | `M_2=77`, `M_3=97` | charged Moh p.202 read |
+| split-side multiplicities | `v_s=8`, `u_s=3` | Moh p.194 top form |
+| major radii | `delta_2=1/3`, `delta_1=4/9` | Moh p.194 formula / p.202 |
+| principal detector order | `ord g(sigma)=9(3delta-8)` | Prop. 6.1 read with `V_r=u_s` |
+| admissible split orders | `delta=2` or `delta=5/2` | charged Opus §3 enumeration |
+| `delta=5/2` root shape | `p=pi(pi^2-c)`, `c!=0` | mu_2 multiset stability |
+| normalized split scale | `c=1` | `pi`-torus gauge |
+| leading `Gbar` face | `p^9` | Xu §8 / charged review |
+| leading `Fbar` face | `p^6` | Xu §8 / approximate-root relation |
+
+Unknown in the executable high-`z` systems:
+
+| item | treatment here |
+|---|---|
+| `Gbar` high-`z` coefficients | variables `g_j_i` listed in JSON `unknown_terms` |
+| `Fbar` high-`z` coefficients | induced from `Gbar^2-Fbar^3=0`; not independent |
+| Jacobian scalar | variable `gamma`, localized by Rabinowitsch |
+| split scale | variable `split_c`, equation `split_c-1`, localized with `gamma` |
+| lower `z` bands | omitted, so no full pair claim |
+| `T2,T3` recurrences | omitted; Prop. 6.2 boxes only cover `T_i` for `i<s` |
+| `e0` in Xu's `q1` | not present in this `Fbar/Gbar` high-band system |
+| final-root coefficient vectors at `delta=3` | only their forced high-face/parity consequences are represented |
+
+The last two omissions are why the output is typed `OPEN`, not a decider.  The
+charged local `delta=5/2` lift tracks `q1` and its additive constant; this
+Prop. 6.2 high-`z` driver does not reconstruct a source-licensed global `T3`
+object, so adding an idle `e0` variable would only inflate the dimension.
+
+The mu_2 condition was imposed as a linear parity condition on coefficients,
+not as choosing one root.  In local ramified variables
+
+```text
+y=s^-2,  z=pi*s^5,
+Gbar=s^-9 sum_q B_q(pi)s^q.
+```
+
+Galois invariance under `(s,pi)->(-s,-pi)` gives
+`B_q(-pi)=(-1)^(q+1) B_q(pi)`.  The builder records the corresponding
+wrong-parity coefficient equations and then prunes the zero columns.
+
+## System
+
+Literal high-`z` depth `d` means using
+`Gbar` bands `z^27,...,z^(28-d)`.  A monomial `y^i z^j` in `Gbar` has local
+order
+
+```text
+q=-2i+5j+9.
+```
+
+Only terms with `0<=q<=d` were kept.  The `q=0` terms are fixed by
+`p(pi)^9=pi^9(pi^2-1)^9`.  For example:
+
+```text
+z^27:  y^72 z^27
+z^25: -9 y^67 z^25
+z^23:  36 y^62 z^23
+```
+
+The `Fbar` bands are induced recursively from the approximate-root relation
+`Gbar^2-Fbar^3=0` in the corresponding high `z` bands:
+
+```text
+F_18=y^48,
+3*y^96*F_(18-r) = [z^(54-r)](Gbar^2 - previously known Fbar^3).
+```
+
+Every approximate-root division had zero remainder in the built systems.
+The Jacobian rows are the coefficients of
+
+```text
+J_{y,z}(Fbar,Gbar)=F_y G_z - F_z G_y
+```
+
+in the visible high `z` bands.  Since the Jacobian is a constant, all these
+positive `z` bands must vanish.
+
+Singular rings used `dp` order and variables in the declared order printed in
+each `.sing` file:
+
+```text
+ring R=char,(Gbar-coefficients,gamma,split_c,T),dp;
+ideal I=Eq, split_c-1, T*gamma*split_c-1;
+```
+
+Controls in every run:
+
+```text
+ideal(split_c,T*gamma*split_c-1)              -> unit
+ideal(split_c-1,gamma-1,T*gamma*split_c-1)    -> nonunit
+ideal(Eq,split_c-1)                           -> nonunit
+```
+
+No bare `sat()` was used.
+
+Equation origins:
+
+| origin | generator form | depth 4 | depth 5 | depth 6 |
+|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| forced top-band Jacobian rows | `g_27_71=0`, `g_27_70=0`; depth 6 also forces `g_27_69=0` through the Jacobian ideal | 2 | 2 | included in 89 |
+| approximate-root divisibility | remainders after division by `3*y^96` | 0 | 0 | 0 |
+| high-`z` Jacobian coefficients | coefficients of `J_{y,z}` in visible positive `z` bands | 0 | 0 | 87 |
+| split-scale gauge/localization | `split_c-1`, `T*gamma*split_c-1` | wrapper | wrapper | wrapper |
+| wrapper controls | empty, nonempty, unsaturated-nonunit controls | pass | pass | pass |
+
+The depth-4/5 systems are therefore very small after the Prop. 6.2/local-order
+support is applied: they only see the two immediate top-band cancellations.
+Depth 6 is the first depth here where the high-`z` Jacobian coefficient rows
+enter nontrivially.
+
+## Results
+
+Depth 4 (`Gbar` bands `27,26,25,24`):
