+## System
+
+Literal high-`z` depth `d` means using
+`Gbar` bands `z^27,...,z^(28-d)`.  A monomial `y^i z^j` in `Gbar` has local
+order
+
+```text
+q=-2i+5j+9.
+```
+
+Only terms with `0<=q<=d` were kept.  The `q=0` terms are fixed by
+`p(pi)^9=pi^9(pi^2-1)^9`.  For example:
+
+```text
+z^27:  y^72 z^27
+z^25: -9 y^67 z^25
+z^23:  36 y^62 z^23
+```
+
+The `Fbar` bands are induced recursively from the approximate-root relation
+`Gbar^2-Fbar^3=0` in the corresponding high `z` bands:
+
+```text
+F_18=y^48,
+3*y^96*F_(18-r) = [z^(54-r)](Gbar^2 - previously known Fbar^3).
+```
+
+Every approximate-root division had zero remainder in the built systems.
+The Jacobian rows are the coefficients of
+
+```text
+J_{y,z}(Fbar,Gbar)=F_y G_z - F_z G_y
+```
+
+in the visible high `z` bands.  Since the Jacobian is a constant, all these
+positive `z` bands must vanish.
+
+Singular rings used `dp` order and variables in the declared order printed in
+each `.sing` file:
+
+```text
+ring R=char,(Gbar-coefficients,gamma,split_c,T),dp;
+ideal I=Eq, split_c-1, T*gamma*split_c-1;
+```
+
+Controls in every run:
+
+```text
+ideal(split_c,T*gamma*split_c-1)              -> unit
+ideal(split_c-1,gamma-1,T*gamma*split_c-1)    -> nonunit
+ideal(Eq,split_c-1)                           -> nonunit
+```
