@@ -0,0 +1,381 @@
+# `(99,66)` delta `5/2` joint high-`z` computation
+
+## Verdict
+
+`OPEN[DELTA-5/2-FULL-JOINT-NOT-KILLED]`.
+
+The executable Prop. 6.2 high-`z` joint systems built here are nonunit through
+depth 6 over `GF(32003)`, `GF(32009)`, `GF(32027)`, and `Q`.  There is no
+`[1]` certificate for `delta=5/2`, so `delta=5/2` is **not** dead from this
+computation and `(99,66)` is **not** reduced to Moh branch B here.
+
+This is a bounded necessary calculation, not a Keller pair and not a full
+polynomial-pair lift.  The missing full pieces are the lower `z` bands, the
+effective `T2,T3 in K[f,g]` recurrences, the major `4/9` centre, and Moh's
+unprinted 11-variable elimination.
+
+Artifacts:
+
+```text
+box/g9966d52-20260903/g9966_delta52_joint_driver.py
+box/g9966d52-20260903/g9966_delta52_joint_results.json
+box/g9966d52-20260903/delta52_highz_depth{4,5,6}_{F32003,F32009,F32027,Q}.sing
+box/g9966d52-20260903/delta52_highz_depth{4,5,6}_{F32003,F32009,F32027,Q}.log
+box/g9966d52-20260903/control_moh1612_appendixII_Q.sing
+box/g9966d52-20260903/control_moh1612_appendixII_Q.log
+box/g9966d52-20260903/artifacts.sha256
+```
+
+## Custody
+
+The lane receipt `xmodel/g9966-delta52-joint-gpt55-20260903.run.v2` was parsed
+mechanically.  The manifest was generated from its indexed
+`charged_input_<i>_basename=` and `charged_input_<i>_sha256=` fields; no digest
+from the prompt was retyped.  The command wrote the derived manifest outside
+the read-only lane input directory and ran `sha256sum -c`.
+
+All ten frozen inputs under `/tmp/jc2-lane.gSx1Ze/inputs` returned `OK`:
+
+```text
+g9966-source-review-opus5-20260903.md
+xu-delta52-lift-gpt55-20260903.md
+moh9966-B-lift-sol56-20260903.md
+moh9966-branchB-sol56-20260903.md
+xu9966-read-gpt55-20260903.md
+triangular_preprocess.py
+moh1983_jram340_configurations_of_roots.pdf
+xu2016_intersection_numbers_split_minor_roots_arxiv1604.07683v4.pdf
+FALLACY-v2.md
+g9966rev_driver.py
+```
+
+## Moh Source Read
+
+Moh page images were generated and named:
+
+```text
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p190_pdf51.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p191_pdf52.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p192_pdf53.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p193_pdf54.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p194_pdf55.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p195_pdf56.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_p196_pdf57.png
+box/g9966d52-20260903/moh_pp190_196_pdf51_57.txt
+```
+
+Read facts:
+
+* p.190 defines the minor-disc branch by the multiplicity inequality against
+  `d_r/(n-M_r)`.  For `(99,66)`, the charged skeleton has `d_3=11`,
+  `n-M_3=2`, so the threshold is `11/2`; `u_3=3` is the minor side and
+  `v_3=8` is the major side.
+* pp.191-193 prove Prop. 6.1.  Read on the minor side with `V_r=u_s=3`,
+  `delta_3=-1`, and `n/d_3=9`, the order identity is
+  `ord g(sigma)=n*delta_3+u_s*(n/d_3)*(delta-delta_3)
+  = -99+27(delta+1)=9(3delta-8)`.  Thus the detector ceiling is
+  `delta<8/3`.
+* p.194 gives the coordinate setup.  The top form is
+  `[(y-a x)^v_s (y-b x)^u_s]^(n/d_s)` with `a != b`; after choosing the major
+  direction so `a=0`, Moh defines `z=y-bx-e`.
+* p.195 states Prop. 6.2:
+  `deg_y Gbar=v_s*n/d_s`, `deg_z Gbar=u_s*n/d_s`, and for `i<s`,
+  `deg_y Tbar_i^psi=v_s*(-mu_i)/d_s`,
+  `deg_z Tbar_i^psi=u_s*(-mu_i)/d_s`.
+* p.196 proof uses the same expression `Gbar=sum a_ij y^i z^j` and the total
+  degree condition `i+j<=n`.
+
+For `(99,66)`, `d_s=11`, `v_s=8`, `u_s=3`, `-mu_1=66`, `-mu_2=55`.
+Therefore N14 is:
+
+```text
+Fbar=T_1^psi in span{y^i z^j: 0<=i<=48, 0<=j<=18, i+j<=66},
+  corner y^48 z^18.
+
+Gbar in span{y^i z^j: 0<=i<=72, 0<=j<=27, i+j<=99},
+  corner y^72 z^27.
+
+T2bar in span{y^i z^j: 0<=i<=40, 0<=j<=15, i+j<=55},
+  corner y^40 z^15.
+```
+
+`T3` is not in Prop. 6.2's printed range (`i<=s-1`), so I did not put a Prop.
+6.2 box on `T3`.
+
+## Branch Data
+
+The charged Opus review §3-§7 was read first.  Its Galois argument is the one
+used here: at ramification denominator `e=2`, the Galois action sends
+`pi -> -pi` and must preserve the root multiset with multiplicities.  A
+`[2,1]` multiset cannot be stable because both the double and simple fixed
+root would have to be `0`.  Thus the `delta=5/2` split is forced to
+`[1,1,1]` with
+
+```text
+p(pi)=pi(pi^2-c),  c != 0.
+```
+
+The gauge `pi -> lambda*pi` sets `c=1`.  I kept a variable `split_c` in the
+Singular localizer and imposed `split_c-1`; saturation used
+`T*gamma*split_c-1`, so both the split scale and Jacobian scalar are localized.
+
